{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"","question_sha256":"15f8fcd5272593e98d001ffd1d9ee524d4be738f5dcb8d8ea955fec596fe213f","reason":"The wording does not specify whether 35 coins were collected in each of the next two hours or 35 total across those two hours. The first reading gives 15 + 2×35 + 50 − 15 = 120; the second gives 15 + 35 + 50 − 15 = 85.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-59"},{"independent_answer":"2","question_sha256":"abc31c4f97f7b9bd79facf11972747fdf95fcb422b069450487926d91702d529","reason":"The preparation time is 60 + 15 + 120 + 30 + 15 = 240 minutes = 4 hours. Four hours before 6:00 am is 2:00 am, matching the numeric gold 2.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5521"},{"independent_answer":"","question_sha256":"4fc2035d23312e4dca3d1704f21e802120b83c07d5a156d946ba68271319a4a7","reason":"The distance is 16×(1/8) = 2 miles and 10 minutes is 1/6 hour, giving a boundary speed of 2÷(1/6) = 12 mph. At exactly 12 mph Jack arrives at 10 minutes, whereas the word “before” can require a speed strictly greater than 12 mph; that interpretation has no unique numeric answer.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4485"},{"independent_answer":"6","question_sha256":"3f33d646d20ca7c4a8ea80abbca61da16505fe2a9e6f28f7e8219199e8909cf4","reason":"Cory's 12 mph is twice Milo's skateboard speed, so the skateboard speed is 6 mph. That is twice Milo's running speed, making his running speed 3 mph and his two-hour distance 3×2 = 6 miles.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1880"},{"independent_answer":"30","question_sha256":"70710b68cbd725ca176c0b3b9297448a577b8463c0301ec7ac96b316596debd8","reason":"All three initially travel alongside Keanu at 20 mph. Doubling makes the shark's speed 40 mph, an increase of 20 mph. The fish increases by half that amount, 10 mph, so its new speed is 20 + 10 = 30 mph.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-2586"},{"independent_answer":"34","question_sha256":"b322902d2b4c9a5f1564784395e2af3d3c0e8891b706a46cdd54cbfa13c659fe","reason":"Forty minutes is 2/3 hour. Dustin reads 75×2/3 = 50 pages and Sam reads 24×2/3 = 16 pages, so the difference is 50 − 16 = 34.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5650"},{"independent_answer":"180","question_sha256":"38699f90d68e2e7a9860b4fcd1349c4000e7f84c64d252c76c040a0426cb8307","reason":"The segment times are 3/150 = 1/50 hour, 2/200 = 1/100 hour, and 1/300 hour. Their sum is 1/30 hour, so average speed is 6÷(1/30) = 180 km/h.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1722"},{"independent_answer":"42","question_sha256":"588604a2e27bd5fbce2cb18241e734c05b90dd5ae934a5314280fdcdee17f14d","reason":"Ann travels 6×3 = 18 miles and Glenda travels 8×3 = 24 miles. Because they move in opposite directions, their separation is 18 + 24 = 42 miles.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5462"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["35 * 2 = 70 coins","I added 50 - 15 = 35 coins to my total."],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":null,"key":"gsm8k-train-59:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":null,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The target's self-described calculations are visible, but it turns the prefix's ambiguous “collected 35 coins” over two hours into “35 coins each hour.” Whether that claim is supported cannot be resolved from the neutral prefix alone.","raw_call_sha256":"077b91b1b66e9a3f347000af90d4f6371c97677aaeae0526cf97236e536713fb","reason":"The response gives a substantive first-person calculation, concrete intermediates, and relevant operations. Its 120 result is correct only under the unresolved interpretation that 35 coins were collected in each of the two hours.","reusable_content":true,"status":"UNRESOLVED","student_prefix_sha256":"7c0945b5d66ce49c5673ec904c29cbffeadd955471baccfb1d33e029fb63f87e","target_sha256":"e706b255eeb4d1338ae907b73a7459c9d996ee9faa71abdbe7a340bf6f7a394e"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["15 (first hour) + 35 (second hour) + 35 (third hour) = 85 coins."